      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}x).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14258704/assets/7955bebdbd0ba4e92f8f56ed8a2ddb6cec57315b20c906b9735f82d1d9e19f0b.png)\n\nAs $x$ increases, the graph oscillates between the values $y=-1$ and $y=1$ indefinitely. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}x)=DNE.\n$$",
