    "q-67725": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67725",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /4)}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /4)}\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+1}{2\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
